; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Os\Os_Hal_Core.c	   306  \ID COV_OS_HALPLATFORMISRMAPPINGAVAILABILITY
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Os\Os_Hal_Core.c	   307    \ACCEPT XX
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Os\Os_Hal_Core.c	   308    \ACCEPT XF
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Os\Os_Hal_Core.c	   309    \REASON As the interrupt mapping functionality is not supported on the TriCore platform, conditions are always false and
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Os\Os_Hal_Core.c	   310            functions will never be called. The unnecessary code parts should be removed by compiler optimization.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Os\Os_Hal_Core.c	   311            As the tests run on each platform the OS is to be released for, we always just test the code for the
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Os\Os_Hal_Core.c	   312            respective platform. No risk as the remaining code shall be optimized away.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Os\Os_Hal_Core.c	   313  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Os\Os_Hal_Core.c	   314  \ID COV_OS_HALPLATFORMFRT16BITAVAILABILITY
